From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:22:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: describe the
 IMX766 focus actuator

The factory camera module of the main camera names its focus actuator
an AK7377. Describe it at 0x0c on the IMX766 CCI bus, powered by the
wide camera VAF regulator with the camera I/O supply as pull-up, and
link it to the sensor through lens-focus. There is no AK7377 support
in the kernel; try it as an AK7375, the closest part of the family the
ak7375 driver handles.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts      | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
index 0d0117ce8..36678a3a3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -1010,7 +1010,17 @@ camu_gt24p128e: eeprom@51 {
 };
 
 &cci1_i2c1 {
-	/* actuator (For Wide sensor) @ 0xc */
+	/*
+	 * AK7377 focus actuator of the IMX766 module (the factory camera module
+	 * names it abra_qtech_ak7377_actuator); driven as an AK7375.
+	 */
+	camw_ak7377: actuator@c {
+		compatible = "asahi-kasei,ak7375";
+		reg = <0x0c>;
+
+		vdd-supply = <&vreg_camw_vaf_1p8>;
+		vio-supply = <&vreg_cam_vio_1p8>;
+	};
 
 	camera@10 {
 		compatible = "sony,imx766";
@@ -1034,6 +1044,8 @@ camera@10 {
 		orientation = <1>; // Rear facing
 		rotation = <90>;
 
+		lens-focus = <&camw_ak7377>;
+
 		port {
 			camera_imx766_ep: endpoint {
 				data-lanes = <1 2 3>;
-- 
